nibOS @VERSION@ (@EDITION@) for the Anbernic RG DS+

nibOS's own code is free software under the GNU GPL, version 3 or later (licenses/
nibos-GPL-3.0.txt; https://github.com/abradburne/nibos, at @NIBOS_COMMIT@); its SDK library,
nibkit, is MIT (licenses/nibkit-MIT.txt).
It is built on Arch Linux ARM and is not affiliated with Arch Linux, Arch Linux ARM or
Anbernic. This image contains the following, each under its own licence; the licence texts
are in /usr/share/licenses/ on the device and in licenses/ on this partition.

Built here, from source
- Linux @KERNEL_COMMIT@ with nibOS's patches: GPL-2.0.
- U-Boot @UBOOT_TAG@ with nibOS's patches (SPL and the fallback U-Boot): GPL-2.0+.
- nibOS's hardware layer (nibos-hw), the boot and goodbye pictures (the splash, with dsboot's
  art) and the safe mode: GPL-3.0-or-later. nibkit, built into DSlot and the emulators: MIT.
- The console font (Terminus, built into the kernel): GPL-2.0, with the kernel.
@EXTRA_COMPONENTS@
Not free software, redistributed under their licences
- Rockchip's DDR init (@RKBIN_DDR@) and TF-A BL31 (@RKBIN_BL31@), from rkbin at
  @RKBIN_COMMIT@ (licenses/rkbin.txt). Built into the bootloader at the start of the card.
- Realtek's Wi-Fi and Bluetooth firmware for the RTL8821CS, from linux-firmware
  (licenses/LICENCE.rtlwifi_firmware.txt; which licence covers which firmware file:
  licenses/WHENCE).

Not included
- The speaker amplifiers' tuning file (Awinic's), which isn't ours to redistribute: see the
  documentation for importing it from your own stock card.

Every Arch Linux ARM package in the image, with its version and licence, is listed in
packages.txt on this partition (and /usr/share/doc/nibos/packages.txt).

Source code
The complete corresponding source for the GPL and LGPL software in this image (nibOS's
trees at the commits above, and the source packages of every GPL and LGPL package listed in
packages.txt) is published with the image at @SOURCE_URL@, and will be for at least three
years after this image was last offered.
